 is all these  are all of the nodes and i could keep  scrolling here but once you get ten in a  row on level one edition then it will  recommend that you do level two edition  mult the next the first level of  multiplication and then level one  subtraction so this these lines show the  dependencies and so you can keep moving  up and up and let me zoom out a little  bit so we can get a better appreciation  for everything and just so you get a  sense of the type of modules that there  are there are things in geometry like  this pythagorean theorem module if you  know how to solve what they're asking  for you can just put the answer in if  you don't know how to solve it you can  say i'd like a hint and you can get the  actual hints  you can get the actual hints for that  type of problem now if you have no clue  of how to do it you can watch the videos  for that type of problem and these are  the related videos right over here let  me show you maybe one more module just  so that we get a sense of the scope over  here so you have modules like this which  are algebra modules if you know how to  do it if you know how to solve for x  type select the answer and there are  other types of there's free answer and  things like that as well  if you don't know how to do it it will  give you the steps for that exact  problem and once again there's an  infinite number of problems it will give  you as many as you need until you can  show your proficient by doing 10 in a  row so the paradigm is ki the student  really just works at their own pace and  really gets motivated through the points  and the game mechanics to go as far as  they can and right now our knowledge map  covers everything from very basic  mathematics from that basic edition well  into high school level mathematics most  of algebra and algebra ii and already a  good amount of trigonometry and  precalculus and even a little bit of  calculus so that's just the what a  student would do on a regular basis but  next i want to show you  kind of the data that the student can  see on him or herself and also what a  teacher or parent can see on the student  so both that this view can be viewed  either by the student or by a mentor a  parent or a teacher so this just shows  the activity over the last few days this  kind of a light green color that shows  the time spent the height is the time  spent on videos on that day sorry the  time the time spent on exercises on that  day and the navy blue shows the time  spent on videos and these show this is  the highest badge achieved and this is  proficiency achieved that day when you  scroll on top of it it gives you more  detail on what happened on that day you  see right here on february 8 2011  4625 energy points 19 total minutes  spent on videos it shows which videos 19  minutes spent on exercises shows the  exercises and it tells the achievements  that the student has achieved now you  can get this over at any time duration  this is the student over the last 30  days  this is actually from a trial we're  doing out here in northern california  where the students are doing this as  part of their classroom so they're doing  it both at home and at night so this is  over the last 30 days you can also see  what the student did yesterday and you  can see it by hour so you can get pretty  granular detail and once again when you  scroll over you see the detail this is  these are the badges that a student  earns and they get more prestigious as  you go to the left your meteorite badges  are pretty easy to get black hole badges  are super hard to get sun badges are  quite hard to get but if we just look at  this students moon badges these are the  ones that they've  these are the badges that he or she has  earned and then here are the possible  badges and these are things that we want  to motivate students to do so if you  become a apprentice arithmetician if you  get proficiency in these modules you can  go transonic which means doing problems  very quickly getting a streak very  quickly on an exercise you can um you  can show that you're persistent any type  of trait that we think are positive  we've been creating badging mechanisms  for  and so there's obviously other badges  earth badges are even more prestigious  sun badges all of the rest once again  all this is available it's free you just  have to log in with the google or  facebook id and we're going to extend  that to other types of ways to log in  and so you could see this just the  activity you can also see focus which is  a read of what the student has been up  to so if you're a parent or a teacher  say hey you know what has  my child been up to and this outer  circle over here shows  the mix of exercises the student has  worked on and if you scroll over it  gives more detail the inner circle shows  the mix of videos and once again it  gives detail by video and you can do it  over different time durations as well  and then you can click on any one of  these you can click on any one of these  to get more detail so in simplifying  radicals students spent 52 minutes in  the last 30 days on this did 89 total  problems 55 correct without a hint but  if you want more granular data and this  is about as granular as you can get you  can actually see all of the problems  that the student has done  all of them so this is this is 50 this  is the 55th problem that the student did  got it wrong  then watched then watched the video and  got some hints then got and the red  means wrong blue means right the height  of the bar means how long it took them  in seconds so they watched a video got  hint got a few right but then started to  get some wrong watch the video again  slowly kind of kind of ironed out the  deficiencies that they would have and  eventually what they were able to get  they were able to get 10 in a row and if  a teacher or student or a parent wants  to know exactly which problem they got  wrong or right you can literally just  click on that bar and