l by itself is for a  student to walk in every day  and they look at a dashboard that shows  where every student is in the class and  the paradigm is  the students who are you know they're  going to be at all different levels so  let me make it clear so this is a  dashboard these are the students right  over here i blanked them out for privacy  reasons  but each row here is a student each  column here is a different concept one  of those stars that you saw in the  knowledge map green means that the  student is proficient already in that  concept let me scroll to the right blue  means that they're working on it but no  cause for concern and then red means  red means that they are probably stuck  so the paradigm for the teacher is is  intervene only when a student is stuck  and that intervention might be a direct  intervention take these two kids aside  and work on multiplying decimals or  there's one student in particular is  having trouble with multiplying decimals  or even better why you take some of  these students here that are already  proficient and pair them up with the  student  first so this is just a a and then we  have other reports there's even a  real-time dashboard of what what exactly  is going on in the classroom in real  time the class isn't going on right now  so i can't show you that dashboard but  we're constantly adding new reports to  really facilitate this paradigm of every  kid learning at their own pace having a  ton of data so that the teacher and the  parent can really leverage their time  optimally to really  focus on students weak points

